The '''2013 FIFA Club World Cup final''' was the final match of the [[2013 FIFA Club World Cup]], an [[association football]] tournament hosted by [[Morocco]]. It was the 10th final of the [[FIFA Club World Cup]], a [[FIFA]]-organised tournament between the winners of the six continental confederations as well as the host nation's league champions.

The final was contested between German club [[FC Bayern Munich|Bayern Munich]], representing [[UEFA]] as the reigning champions of the [[UEFA Champions League]], and Moroccan club [[Raja CA|Raja Casablanca]], representing the host country as the reigning champions of the [[Botola]]. It was played at the [[Stade de Marrakech]] in [[Marrakesh]] on 21 December 2013.<ref>{{cite news |title=Bayern breeze into CWC final |url=http://espnfc.com/uk/en/report/383397/report.html?soccernet=true&cc=5739 |work=ESPN FC |publisher=ESPN Internet Ventures |date=17 December 2013 |access-date=19 December 2013 }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=Raja Casablanca 3-1 Atletico Mineiro |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/0/football/25391214 |publisher=BBC Sport (British Broadcasting Corporation) |date=18 December 2013 |access-date=19 December 2013 }}</ref>

==Background==

===Bayern Munich===
[[FC Bayern Munich|Bayern Munich]] qualified for the tournament as winners of the [[2012–13 UEFA Champions League]], following a 2–1 win against [[Borussia Dortmund]] in the [[2013 UEFA Champions League Final|final]]. This was Bayern Munich's first time competing in the tournament. They twice won the [[Intercontinental Cup (1960–2004)|Intercontinental Cup]], the predecessor of the FIFA Club World Cup, in [[1976 Intercontinental Cup|1976]] and [[2001 Intercontinental Cup|2001]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/sports/soccer/2013/12/17/club-world-cup-bayern-munich-english-league-cup-sunderland-manchester-city/4083501/ |title=Bayern Munich cruises into Club World Cup final |work=USA Today|date=2013-12-16 |access-date=2013-12-20}}</ref> They reached the final after defeating Chinese club [[Guangzhou Evergrande F.C.|Guangzhou Evergrande]] in the semi-finals.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/25425116 |title=Bayern Munich through to Fifa Club World Cup final with 3-0 win |publisher=BBC |date=2013-12-16 |access-date=2013-12-20}}</ref>

===Raja Casablanca===
[[Raja CA|Raja Casablanca]] won the [[2012–13 Botola]] to earn the host country berth of the tournament. This was Raja Casablanca's second time competing in the tournament, having participated in the competition in the inaugural edition in [[2000 FIFA Club World Championship|2000]]. They were the second team to reach the final of the competition (after [[Sport Club Corinthians Paulista|Corinthians]] in [[2000 FIFA Club World Championship Final|2000]]) under the condition of being the host nation's national champions,<ref>{{cite news |first=Karl |last=Matchett |title=Raja Casablanca vs. Atletico Mineiro: Score, Grades and Post-Match Reaction |url=https://bleacherreport.com/articles/1893764-raja-casablanca-vs-atletico-mineiro-score-grades-and-post-match-reaction |publisher=Bleacher Report |date=18 December 2013 |access-date=20 December 2013 }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |first=Kevin |last=McCauley |title=Raja Casablanca vs. Atletico Mineiro: Final score 3-1, Moroccan champions will face Bayern Munich |url=https://www.sbnation.com/soccer/2013/12/18/5224874/raja-casablanca-vs-atletico-mineiro--2013-club-world-cup-final-score-result |publisher=SBNation.com (Vox Media) |date=16 December 2013 |access-date=20 December 2013 }}</ref> as well as the second African finalist (after [[TP Mazembe]] in [[2010 FIFA Club World Cup Final|2010]]).<ref>{{cite news |title=Raja shock Atletico to reach final |url=http://www.cafonline.com/football/news/18950-raja-shock-atletico-to-reach-final.html |publisher=cafonline.com (Confederation of African Football) |date=19 December 2013 |access-date=21 April 2014 }}</ref> They reached the final after defeating New Zealand club [[Auckland City FC|Auckland City]] in the play-off round,<ref>{{cite news |title=Raja score late to beat Auckland |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/25318591 |publisher=BBC Sport (British Broadcasting Corporation) |date=12 December 2013 |access-date=20 December 2013 }}</ref> Mexican club [[C.F. Monterrey|Monterrey]] in the quarter-finals,<ref>{{cite news |title=Raja Casablanca reach Club World Cup semi-final |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/25390412 |publisher=BBC Sport (British Broadcasting Corporation) |date=15 December 2013 |access-date=20 December 2013 }}</ref> and Brazilian club [[Clube Atlético Mineiro|Atletico Mineiro]] in the semi-finals.<ref>{{cite news |first=Ian |last=Hughes |title=Raja revel in historic victory |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/25451200 |publisher=BBC Sport (British Broadcasting Corporation) |date=19 December 2013 |access-date=20 December 2013 }}</ref>

